  "body": "## pm-stack backups silently produced empty day-dirs for 3 days\n\n`~/backups/pm-stack/` has day directories for 2026-10-30, 2026-10-31, and 2026-11-01 that were created on schedule but contain **no archive** — the last good tarball before today was 2026-10-29. Nothing alarmed; the gap was found by hand during the 2026-11-01 Kaneo/PostgreSQL incident (#3849), where the Oct 29 `kaneo.dump` turned out to be the only logical fallback.\n\nCause: `~/tools/pm-stack-backup.sh` creates the day dir up front, then `set -e` kills it mid-run, leaving the empty dir as camouflage. The mid-run deaths were stale container names from the compose→oci migrations: `docker exec pm-stack-postgres-1` failed while the compose stack was down for the pm-apps activation (Oct 30), and after Grist/Pad became oci containers the script still targeted `grist-grist-1` / `pad-pad-1` (live names: `pm-grist` / `pm-pad`).\n\nAlready fixed on the laptop (2026-11-01): names updated in `~/tools/pm-stack-backup.sh` (original kept as `pm-stack-backup.sh.orig-2026-11-01`), and a rerun produced a verified archive for 2026-11-01 (manifest-checked by the script itself, sha256 d7a8881df26333269d4cb9b732b3daafbb5a6fdf8a7ee18a084d1baae7551833).\n\nWhat remains worth doing:\n- The script (or its scheduling service, code#1516) should treat \"day dir exists but no verified archive\" as a failure worth surfacing — an empty dir currently reads as a completed backup day in any casual listing.\n- Container names are migration-fragile; resolving targets by label/project (or failing with the container list in the log) would have made this a one-day, self-explaining failure instead of a silent 3-day gap.\n\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A backup run that ends without a verified archive is surfaced as a failure (alarm, non-zero service result, or filed issue) — an empty day-dir no longer reads as a completed backup day.\n- Backup targets are resolved robustly against container renames (by label/project, or the run fails loudly with the actual container list in the log), so a compose-to-oci migration cannot silently break targeting again.\n- A drill or log excerpt demonstrates the failure path firing on a simulated missing-container run.\n",
